1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:02,030
You're looking at a British general wounded

2
00:00:02,030 --> 00:00:04,590
9 times. Any one of them should have killed

3
00:00:04,590 --> 00:00:07,320
him. So why did he say he enjoyed the war?

4
00:00:07,750 --> 00:00:09,570
Adrian Carton de Wiart.

5
00:00:09,570 --> 00:00:10,790
At 19, he quits Oxford,

6
00:00:10,790 --> 00:00:12,650
lies about his name and age,

7
00:00:12,650 --> 00:00:14,100
and sails to the Boer War.

8
00:00:14,590 --> 00:00:16,800
First wound: a bullet in the stomach.

9
00:00:17,150 --> 00:00:20,600
1914, Somaliland. Storming a desert fort,

10
00:00:20,650 --> 00:00:22,080
he is shot twice in the face.

11
00:00:22,530 --> 00:00:23,350
He loses an eye,

12
00:00:23,350 --> 00:00:24,380
and part of an ear.

13
00:00:24,633 --> 00:00:25,933
He puts on a black eye patch,

14
00:00:25,933 --> 00:00:27,303
and sails for France.

15
00:00:27,708 --> 00:00:30,898
1915. A shell shatters his left hand.

16
00:00:31,248 --> 00:00:33,428
The doctor won't cut off his dangling fingers,

17
00:00:33,428 --> 00:00:34,998
so he pulls them off himself.

18
00:00:35,306 --> 00:00:37,476
Later, the surgeons take the whole hand.

19
00:00:37,833 --> 00:00:41,393
1916, the Somme. He pulls grenade pins with

20
00:00:41,393 --> 00:00:43,863
his teeth. When three other commanders fall,

21
00:00:44,033 --> 00:00:45,073
he leads all their men,

22
00:00:45,073 --> 00:00:46,743
and wins the Victoria Cross.

23
00:00:47,854 --> 00:00:49,244
Then he's shot through the skull.

24
00:00:49,714 --> 00:00:50,624
The ankle. The hip.

25
00:00:50,714 --> 00:00:51,724
The leg. The ear.

26
00:00:52,194 --> 00:00:53,984
Every time, he goes back to the front.

27
00:00:54,343 --> 00:00:58,283
1941. Aged 60, his bomber crashes into the

28
00:00:58,283 --> 00:01:00,263
sea off Libya. He swims ashore,

29
00:01:00,263 --> 00:01:01,193
and is captured.

30
00:01:01,572 --> 00:01:03,222
In an Italian castle prison,

31
00:01:03,652 --> 00:01:05,282
he digs a tunnel for seven months.

32
00:01:05,606 --> 00:01:07,376
Once, he stays free for eight days,

33
00:01:07,946 --> 00:01:09,336
disguised as an Italian peasant.

34
00:01:09,946 --> 00:01:11,536
He's 62, with one eye,

35
00:01:11,566 --> 00:01:13,456
one hand, and he can't speak Italian.

36
00:01:13,902 --> 00:01:14,702
He died in bed,

37
00:01:14,702 --> 00:01:16,792
at 83. And in his memoir,

38
00:01:16,922 --> 00:01:19,252
he wrote: "Frankly, I had enjoyed the war."

39
00:01:19,589 --> 00:01:21,789
Who was tougher? Name one soldier below,

40
00:01:21,789 --> 00:01:23,519
and follow Buried Chronicles.

